UPDATE companies SET description='Classic Sofa of NY traces its roots to 1982, when the company opened its first factory in Brooklyn and began hand-crafting benchmade furniture for the tri-state area. After the 2008 recession forced a consolidation of its five retail locations, the business refocused on production integrity. In 2012, Blake Anding acquired the brand, assuming the roles of president and head of design, and relocated manufacturing to a dedicated facility at 728 East 136th Street in the Bronx.

The company produces custom upholstered furniture, drapery, and large-scale soft furnishings using locally sourced hardwood frames assembled with traditional joinery. Every piece is built in-house by a team of master artisans and apprentices, allowing the firm to control quality from frame construction through final upholstery. The Bronx factory also handles custom wall coverings, window treatments, and full interior outfitting for hospitality, yacht, and private-jet projects.

Clients include residential customers, interior designers (trade), and commercial accounts such as hotels and private aviation operators. The firm offers in-home consultations, progress sit-tests, and white-glove delivery with on-site installation, supporting projects from single-piece commissions to full-suite fit-outs.

Classic Sofa differentiates itself with a lifetime frame guarantee, a commitment to eco-friendly materials, and a vertical operation that keeps design and manufacturing under one roof. The brand cites its Savile Row–inspired attention to detail and the preservation of old-world craft methods as the foundation of its longevity.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom upholstered furniture manufacturing", "Drapery fabrication", "Benchmade furniture construction", "In-home consultation and measurement", "Progress sit-testing", "On-site build and installation", "White-glove delivery", "Large-scale upholstered furnishings", "Custom wall coverings", "Window treatment fabrication", "Full-service interior outfitting", "Hospitality furniture production", "Yacht and private jet interior outfitting"], "industries": ["Residential", "Trade (interior design)", "Commercial", "Hospitality", "Yachts", "Private jets", "Interior design"], "materials": ["Locally sourced hardwoods", "Eco-friendly raw materials"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Lifetime frame guarantee", "Benchmade construction with locally sourced hardwoods", "Vertical in-house design and production at Bronx factory", "Savile Row\u2013level attention to detail", "Eco-friendly materials and production methods"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1982 in Brooklyn -> /about", "Bronx factory at 728 E. 136th Street -> /, /about", "Blake Anding acquired company in 2012 as President and Head of Design -> /about", "Madeline B. Monaghan leads creative direction -> /about", "Benchmade, bespoke furniture handcrafted by master artisans -> /, /about", "Lifetime frame guarantee -> /, /about", "Vertical operation: design and production in-house at Bronx factory -> /about", "Old-world techniques, Savile Row-level attention -> /", "Eco-friendly raw materials and production methods -> /about", "Serves custom residential, trade, and commercial clients -> /", "Specialty projects for hospitality, yachts, private jets -> /", "Exclusive services: in-home consultations, progress sit-tests, on-site build, installation, white-glove delivery -> /", "Showrooms in Manhattan, Palm Beach, Nantucket -> /", "Five retail locations prior to 2008 recession -> /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "benchmade, bespoke furniture expertly handcrafted in New York City since 1982", "founded_year": "1982", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='classic-sofa-of-ny' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Clauser Furniture operates a retail showroom in Berne, Indiana, offering a broad selection of home furnishings. The company presents itself as a destination for American-made solid wood furniture, with a notable emphasis on pieces crafted by Amish artisans. The company''s website includes an "Our Company" section, though detailed history such as founding year and ownership structure are not provided in the available content.

The product assortment spans living room, bedroom, dining room, home office, and entertainment categories. Specific items include sofas, sectionals, tables, chairs, loveseats, chaises, desks, entertainment centers, chests, dressers, cabinets, bookcases, settees, benches, ottomans, and stools. The store also carries mattresses and a range of decor accessories, and its website provides a mattress finder tool and design idea galleries to assist shoppers.

Clauser Furniture primarily serves residential customers looking for domestically produced solid wood furniture. The physical showroom in Berne allows buyers to view and select pieces in person, while the online catalog extends the reach beyond the local area.

The company distinguishes itself by highlighting its commitment to American-made and Amish-built products, positioning its inventory as solid hardwood furnishings crafted using traditional methods. This focus on domestic sourcing and craftsmanship is presented as a core value proposition.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Retail furniture sales", "Amish furniture sourcing", "Mattress selection assistance", "Design inspiration resources"], "industries": [], "materials": ["Solid hardwood"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["American-made solid wood furniture", "Amish-crafted product lines", "Broad assortment across living room, bedroom, dining, home office, and mattresses", "Mattress finder tool for personalized selection"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Berne, Indiana -> db", "Retail showroom offering living room, bedroom, dining, home office, entertainment, mattress, and decor categories -> page \"/\"", "Emphasis on American-made solid wood furniture -> page \"/\"", "Amish-made product lines -> page \"/\"", "Mattress Finder tool for personalized selection -> page \"/\"", "Design idea galleries -> page \"/\""], "company_type": "Retailer", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Shop at Clauser Furniture in Berne, IN for Sofas, Sectionals, Tables, Chairs, Loveseats, Chaises, Desks, Entertainment Centers, Chests and Dressers, Cabinets, Bookcases, Settees, Benches, Ottomans, Stools.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='clauser-furniture' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Clear-Vu Lighting operates from a 100,000-square-foot facility in Central Islip, New York. The company traces its roots to 1957 when LaMar Lighting was founded in Garden City South. The Clear-Vu brand was launched in 2008 by Autronic Plastics, and the two legacies merged in 2020 when Autronic Plastics acquired LaMar Lighting, consolidating operations under one roof. The business is led by founder and CEO Daniel Lax, who brings 18 years of LED fixture development experience.

The company engineers and manufactures American-made LED lighting systems for demanding environments. Its vertically integrated facility houses in-house plastic injection molding, CNC tooling, LED assembly lines, optical testing stations, and an R&D lab. With 78-plus product lines across six specialized markets, Clear-Vu produces fixtures for transit, construction, commercial, healthcare, life sciences, and correctional applications. The facility operates under ISO 9001:2015 certification.

Clear-Vu serves agencies, institutions, and Fortune 500 companies nationwide. Concrete examples include the NYC Metropolitan Transportation Authority for 15 subway stations under the Enhanced Station Initiative, healthcare facilities requiring surgical illumination with 95+ CRI, pharmaceutical cleanrooms rated ISO3 through ISO8, and correctional facilities needing ligature-resistant, tamper-proof fixtures. The company also supplies low-voltage temporary site lighting for construction, achieving 90 percent energy savings versus traditional systems.

The company emphasizes vertical integration — no outsourcing, no overseas dependencies — as a core differentiator, allowing engineers to walk to the production floor, prototype, test, and begin production without leaving the building. It also highlights BABA/BAA compliance, union-made labor, and direct engineering support from the designers as reasons customers specify its fixtures.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','UL Listed','DLC Listed','BABA/BAA Compliant','NSF P442','LEED']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["In-house plastic injection molding", "In-house CNC tooling and mold making", "LED assembly and testing", "Optical testing and validation", "R&D prototyping and custom fixture design", "DALI emergency backup system integration", "Wireless monitoring (clearNET) deployment", "Low-voltage temporary site lighting systems", "Motion sensor lighting (Occu-Smart) technology", "Cleanroom-rated fixture manufacturing (ISO3\u2013ISO8)", "Vandal-resistant and tamper-proof fixture manufacturing", "Ligature-resistant fixture manufacturing"], "industries": ["Transit / Transportation", "Construction", "Commercial & Industrial", "Healthcare", "Life Sciences / Pharmaceutical", "Correctional & Secure Facilities"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Injection molding presses", "CNC tooling equipment", "LED assembly lines", "Optical testing stations", "R&D lab"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Vertically integrated manufacturing with in-house injection molding, tooling, and assembly", "BABA/BAA compliant for federal projects", "Union-made in the USA", "ISO 9001:2015 certified quality management", "Direct engineering support from the design team"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1957 as LaMar Lighting in Garden City South, NY -> /about-us", "Clear-Vu brand launched 2008 by Autronic Plastics -> /about-us", "Autronic Plastics acquired LaMar Lighting 2020, consolidated in Central Islip -> /about-us", "100,000 sq ft facility in Central Islip, NY -> /, /about-us", "Vertically integrated: injection molding, tooling, LED assembly, optical testing, R&D lab -> /, /about-us", "78+ product lines, 6 specialized markets -> /, /about-us", "ISO 9001:2015 certified -> /, /about-us", "BABA/BAA compliant, Union Made, DLC Listed -> /, /about-us", "CEO Daniel Lax, 18 years LED experience -> /about-us", "130+ years combined team experience -> /about-us", "NYC MTA Enhanced Station Initiative: 15 stations, 20+ custom fixtures -> /", "Healthcare: surgical illumination, 95+ CRI -> /", "Life Sciences: ISO3\u2013ISO8 cleanroom rated -> /", "Correctional: ligature-resistant, tamper-proof -> /", "Construction: FLEX SLS low-voltage temp lighting, 90% energy savings -> /", "Commercial: 78+ product lines, 500,000+ Occu-Smart units installed -> /", "Awards: Made in NY Manufacturing Excellence 2023, BAA Compliance Leadership 2022, NSF P442 First Certification 2021, LEED Innovation 2018, US Patent PLB-01 2014 -> /", "Certifications array: ISO9001, ULLISTED, ISO 9001, BAA COMPLIANT, LEED -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Engineered, manufactured, and supported from our Long Island, New York facility. Vertically Integrated Manufacturing \u2014 In-house plastic injection molding, tooling, engineering, and LED assembly \u2014 all under one roof in Central Islip, NY.", "founded_year": "1957", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='clear-vu-lighting' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Clearloop Corporation is based in Nashville, Tennessee. Founded by three Tennesseans—Bob Corney, Laura Zapata, and founding chairman Gov. Phil Bredesen—the company began as a carbon solution aimed at delivering the environmental, health, and economic benefits of clean energy to communities that need them most, starting in their own backyard. Clearloop was later acquired by Silicon Ranch, one of the largest independent power producers in the United States, to scale its mission.

Instead, it provides a carbon solutions platform that helps organizations measure, reclaim, and track their carbon footprints by funding the construction of new solar energy facilities. The company’s model directs investment toward solar projects in carbon-intense regions of the U.S. South—including sites in Arcadia, Louisiana; Jackson, Tennessee; Panola County, Mississippi; Paris, Tennessee; and White Pine, Tennessee—where new renewable capacity displaces fossil-fuel generation. The acquisition by Silicon Ranch provides the project development and operational backbone to deliver these projects at scale.

The company works with organizations of all sizes, from global corporations to small businesses and educational institutions.

Clearloop differentiates itself by building new solar projects rather than purchasing renewable energy credits from existing installations. It focuses on communities traditionally left behind in the energy transition, aiming to maximize both carbon reduction and local economic benefit. The company states that its fee structure—a percentage of the product’s carbon footprint—funds project construction directly, and that every investment is tracked to show tangible clean energy generation over a 40-year project life.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Carbon footprint measurement", "Carbon offsetting via new solar project development", "Solar project development in underserved communities", "Corporate carbon tracking and reporting", "Scalable carbon reclamation for products and services"], "industries": ["Corporate sustainability", "Clean energy", "Carbon markets", "Solar energy", "Education institutions", "Global corporations", "Small businesses"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Builds new solar projects instead of buying from existing ones", "Targets carbon-intense regions in the U.S. South for maximum emission reduction", "Offers scalable carbon reclamation for any product, product line, or process", "Tracks each corporate investment to show real-time clean energy generation", "Backed by Silicon Ranch, a major independent power producer, for project execution at scale"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters: Nashville, Tennessee -> /about", "Founders: Bob Corney, Laura Zapata, Gov. Phil Bredesen -> /about", "Acquired by Silicon Ranch -> /about", "Business model: carbon solutions via new solar projects -> /about, /", "Project locations: Arcadia LA, Jackson TN, Panola County MS, Paris TN, White Pine TN -> /, /about", "Team members listed -> /about", "Customer types: global corporations, small businesses, educational institutions -> /about", "Differentiators: build new projects, focus on underserved communities, fee based on carbon footprint, tracking over 40 years -> /about", "LinkedIn URL -> db"], "company_type": "Other", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Clearloop creates carbon solutions for organizations of all sizes... to decarbonize the economy, expand access to clean energy, and accelerate the development of new solar projects", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/clearloop-corporation/"], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='clearloop-corporation' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Click Bond is headquartered in Carson City, Nevada. The company focuses on adhesive-bonded fastening solutions.

Its product portfolio includes ACRES® sleeves, rivetless nutplates, bushings, mounts, studs, standoffs, and adhesives. The company offers custom engineering services to develop tailored fastening solutions for specific design challenges.

The company serves a broad range of industries across air, sea, land, and industrial markets. In aviation, its fasteners are used in commercial, military, and general aviation, as well as business jets, advanced air mobility, rotorcraft, unmanned systems, satellites, missiles, and engines. In marine and naval sectors, applications include offshore and naval vessels. Ground transportation markets cover military vehicles, heavy trucks, automotive, rail, and transit. Industrial and green energy sectors also rely on Click Bond products for cable and wiring management, fuel and fluid tanks, interiors, pressurized vessels, decking, equipment attachment, tubing, hoses, repairs, panels, and systems attachment.

Click Bond emphasizes its engineering-driven approach, stating that its engineers pioneer advanced fastening solutions to solve design challenges and enable customer ideas. The company highlights a deep product database with hundreds of iterative designs not publicly listed, supporting customized solutions beyond standard catalog offerings.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Adhesive-bonded fastener manufacturing", "Custom fastener design", "Engineering support"], "industries": ["Commercial Aviation", "Military Aviation", "General Aviation", "Business Jets", "Advanced Air Mobility", "Rotorcraft", "Unmanned Systems", "Satellites", "Missiles", "Engines", "Marine", "Offshore", "Naval", "Military Vehicles", "Heavy Trucks", "Automotive", "Rail", "Transit", "Industrial", "Green Energy"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Customized fastening solutions with extensive iterative product database", "Engineering-driven design for advanced fastening challenges", "Global sales representative network"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters: Carson City, Nevada -> db", "Product focus: adhesive-bonded fasteners -> /", "Markets served: Commercial Aviation, Military Aviation, General Aviation, Business Jets, Advanced Air Mobility, Rotorcraft, Unmanned, Satellites, Missiles, Engines, Marine, Offshore, Naval, Military Vehicles, Heavy Trucks, Automotive, Rail, Transit, Industrial, Green Energy -> /", "Product lines: ACRES\u00ae Sleeves, Rivetless Nutplates, Bushings, Mounts, Studs & Standoffs, Adhesives -> /", "Applications: Cables & Wiring, Fuel & Fluid Tanks, Interiors, Pressurized Vessels, Decking & Floorboards, Equipment Attachment, Tubing & Hoses, Repairs, Panels, Systems Attachment -> /", "Custom solutions: engineers pioneer advanced fastening solutions, hundreds of iterative products not shown online -> /", "Global rep network: reps have locations around the world -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Click Bond, Inc. - Adhesive-Bonded Fasteners For Aerospace, Defense, Marine, Automotive, Rail, Energy, & Industrial Sectors", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='click-bond' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Club Ride Apparel is based in Hailey, Idaho, in the Wood River Valley near Sun Valley. The company was founded in 2008 by Mike Herlinger, who conceived the brand while working at an outdoor store and racing mountain bikes on weekends. Herlinger wanted clothing that reflected the lifestyle of mountain bikers, hikers, raft guides, and ski bums who build their lives around outdoor pursuits in mountain towns.

The brand designs and sells mountain lifestyle apparel for men and women, including technical cycling shirts, flannels, jackets, shorts, pants, and chamois. The line blends performance fabrics with Western-inspired details such as pearl snaps and relaxed fits, aiming to blur the line between on-bike function and off-bike style.

The primary customers are outdoor enthusiasts—mountain bikers, hikers, rafters, and skiers—who value technical performance without sacrificing personality. Products are sold direct-to-consumer through the company’s website and through a network of retail locations across the U.S.

Herlinger started the company after a ride in Sun Valley when he realized he didn’t want to change out of his vintage Western shirt to meet friends. That moment drove the conviction that cycling gear could be both technical and stylish. Today, Club Ride emphasizes irreverent style, durable construction, and mountain-town authenticity as its defining characteristics.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom apparel"], "industries": ["Mountain biking", "Hiking", "Rafting", "Skiing", "Outdoor lifestyle"], "materials": ["Technical fabrics", "Flannel", "Cotton"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": [], "facts_used": ["Founded by Mike Herlinger in 2008 -> /about-us", "Headquarters in Hailey, Idaho -> db", "Offers custom apparel program -> /about-us", "Sells men''s and women''s mountain lifestyle clothing -> /", "Emphasizes technical fabrics with Western-inspired details -> /about-us", "Rider-owned brand -> /", "Free ground shipping on US orders over $125 -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We make apparel for riders who live their lives on two wheels and never take themselves too seriously on the bike or off.", "founded_year": "2008", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='club-ride-apparel' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
