The company operates Coal Creek Station, described as North Dakota''s most efficient power plant, employing approximately 200 people. Its activities span electricity generation, transmission, wind energy integration, and carbon capture initiatives.

Rainbow Energy Center serves the energy sector, providing reliable power to communities and the grid. The company emphasizes local procurement, citing Captain''s Cabin as a community vendor, and highlights its role in supporting the surrounding economy through wages and local partnerships.

