UPDATE companies SET description='Colite Technologies was founded in 2018 in Columbia, South Carolina. The company began as a commercial solar provider dedicated to helping commercial and industrial customers incorporate sustainable energy solutions into their operations.

As a full-service distributed energy solutions provider, Colite designs and delivers customized solar, battery, and hybrid energy systems. Its services span commercial solar installation, energy storage, solar system design, energy resilience and microgrids, maintenance and monitoring, and project financing and ownership structures such as PPAs and leases. The company handles permitting, interconnection paperwork, non-penetrative roof installations, and ground-mounted arrays. Project sizes in its portfolio range from 121 kW to 661 kW, with systems carrying a 5-year workmanship warranty and 10- to 25-year component warranties.

Notable installations include a 121 kW system for Coca-Cola Bottling United, a 197 kW system for Extra Space Storage, a 203 kW system for CubeSmart Self Storage, a 287 kW system for Peach State Trucking, and a 661 kW rooftop solar plus 60 kWh battery project for Sportsman Boats in Summerville, SC. Other clients include Clemson University, SCRA, Nephron Pharmaceuticals, and Dominion Energy.

The company states its mission is to deliver cutting-edge solar solutions that enhance performance, cut costs, and promote environmental responsibility, guided by principles of integrity, innovation, and customer success. It differentiates itself by managing the full project lifecycle — from incentive navigation and financing through engineering, construction, and ongoing monitoring — to help businesses achieve energy independence and resilience.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Commercial solar installation", "Energy storage system integration", "Solar system design and engineering", "Energy resilience and microgrid integration", "Maintenance and real-time monitoring", "Project financing and ownership structures (PPAs, leases, direct ownership)", "Off-grid renewable lighting systems", "EV charging equipment installation", "Permitting and interconnection management", "Non-penetrative roof mounting", "Ground-mounted solar array installation", "Third-party system repair and recommissioning"], "industries": ["Manufacturing", "Distribution & Logistics", "Agriculture", "Corporate Real Estate", "Education", "Government & Research", "Healthcare", "Retail", "Hospitality", "Food & Beverage", "Pharmaceuticals", "Utilities"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Full lifecycle management from incentive navigation to ongoing monitoring", "Non-penetrative roof installations for flat and low-slope roofs", "Comprehensive pre- and post-installation roof inspections", "Real-time monitoring with proactive maintenance dispatch", "Flexible financing options including direct ownership, PPAs, and leases"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2018 -> db", "Headquartered in Columbia, South Carolina -> db", "Full-service distributed energy solutions provider -> /", "Services: commercial solar installation, energy storage, solar system design, energy resilience & microgrids, maintenance & monitoring, project financing & ownership -> /", "Non-penetrative installations for flat and low-slope roofs -> /", "Comprehensive pre- and post-installation roof inspections -> /", "Ground-mounted solar solutions -> /", "Full management of permitting and interconnection paperwork -> /", "5-year workmanship warranty and 10-25 year component warranties -> /", "Case study: 121 kW system for Coca-Cola Bottling United -> /", "Case study: 197 kW system for Extra Space Storage -> /", "Case study: 203 kW system for CubeSmart Self Storage -> /", "Case study: 287.1 kW system for Peach State Trucking -> /", "Case study: 661 kW rooftop solar + 60 kWh battery for Sportsman Boats -> /", "Clients include Clemson University, SCRA, Nephron Pharmaceuticals, Dominion Energy -> /", "Mission: deliver cutting-edge solar solutions that enhance performance, cut costs, promote environmental responsibility -> /", "Principles: integrity, innovation, customer success -> /"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "We design and deliver customized solar, battery, and hybrid energy systems that reduce operating costs, improve resilience, and create long-term energy independence.", "founded_year": "2018", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='colite-technologies' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Colonial Wire & Cable of NJ traces its roots to 1944 in Edison, New Jersey, where it began serving the electrical distribution market. Now a third-generation, family-owned and family-run business, the company operates from its headquarters in Edison and a second manufacturing facility in Hauppauge, New York.

The company manufactures copper electrical building wire for residential, commercial, and industrial applications. Its two state-of-the-art facilities produce residential cable and wiring on Long Island and commercial products in Edison, supplying electrical distributors and wholesalers across North America. All products are made in the United States and carry Underwriters Laboratory approval, with compliance to ASTM, ICEA, IEEE, NEMA, NFPA, and NEC standards.

Colonial Wire & Cable sells directly to electrical distributors and wholesalers, eliminating middlemen. Its customer base spans commercial construction, industrial projects, and residential wiring jobs throughout the U.S. and Canada. The company emphasizes an extensive inventory, high fill rates, and rapid order fulfillment.

Founded on the principle of the Colonial Minutemen—rapid deployment and immediate response—the business differentiates itself through short lead times, direct manufacturer access, and a commitment to personal service with a real person answering every call. Family ownership and UL-verified quality underscore its market position.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Copper electrical building wire manufacturing", "Residential cable manufacturing", "Commercial wire manufacturing", "UL compliance testing", "Direct distribution to wholesalers"], "industries": ["Electrical distribution", "Commercial construction", "Industrial construction", "Residential construction", "Wholesale electrical supply"], "materials": ["Copper"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Direct manufacturer with no middlemen", "All products made in the USA", "Short lead times and prompt response inspired by Minutemen philosophy", "Family-owned, third-generation operation with live phone support"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1944 -> db", "Headquarters Edison, NJ -> db", "Family-owned third generation -> /about-us", "Two manufacturing facilities: Hauppauge NY and Edison NJ -> /about-us", "Products made in USA -> / and /about-us", "Serves electrical distributors and wholesalers nationwide -> / and /about-us", "UL approved/verified -> /about-us", "Direct manufacturer, no middlemen -> /about-us", "Prompt response, short lead times -> /", "Industry associations: ASTM, ICEA, IEEE, NEMA, UL, NFPA, NEC -> /", "Copper electrical building wire -> /", "Residential and commercial products -> / and /about-us"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "With all our products proudly made in the USA, we serve electrical distributors nationwide from two state-of-the-art manufacturing facilities", "founded_year": "1944", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "s