UPDATE companies SET description='Complexus Medical traces its roots to 1968 when F&F Machine Specialties opened as a small tool-and-die shop in a Mishawaka, Indiana basement. The company rebranded as Complexus Medical and, under the leadership of Michael Behrens, has grown into a full-service contract manufacturer with two modern facilities in Mishawaka and Plymouth, Indiana. A 2013 expansion doubled the Mishawaka headquarters, and a second site was added in 2021 to support increasing demand.

The company provides end-to-end contract manufacturing for medical devices and healthcare products. Its service portfolio covers clean-room assembly, sub-assembly and final assembly, custom kitting and sterile barrier packaging, sterilization coordination (EtO, gamma, and e-beam), supply chain management, regulatory support, and rapid prototyping with tooling development. Complexus handles all welding, finishing, and assembly in-house, enabling control over quality and lead times. The firm reports more than 500 products manufactured and emphasizes FDA-compliant documentation throughout.

Complexus serves medical device OEMs, with a historic focus on the orthopedic device and implant industry. Customers rely on the company for complex instruments that involve multiple components, tight tolerances, and intricate geometry. Typical projects include surgical instrument assemblies, procedure packs, tray configurations, and sterile barrier systems that require validated sterilization processes.

The company positions itself on three differentiators: decades of experience with difficult orthopedic instruments, full in-house control of welding, finishing, and assembly, and a "right-sized" structure that is small enough to manage every project detail yet large enough to deliver at scale. These factors, combined with full-service sterilization coordination and two Indiana locations, form the basis of its value proposition.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 13485']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Clean room assembly", "Sub-assembly and final assembly", "Lot traceability", "Device history records", "Custom kit assembly", "Sterile barrier packaging", "Procedure packs", "Tray configurations", "EtO sterilization coordination", "Gamma irradiation coordination", "E-beam sterilization coordination", "Sterilization validation support", "Vendor qualification", "Inventory management", "Just-in-time delivery", "Demand forecasting", "Design history file preparation", "Technical file preparation", "Risk management (ISO 14971)", "Post-market surveillance support", "Rapid prototyping", "Tooling design", "Pilot production runs", "Design for manufacturability", "In-house welding", "In-house finishing"], "industries": ["Medical Devices", "Orthopedic Devices", "Orthopedic Implants", "Healthcare Products"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["55+ years of manufacturing experience (founded 1968)", "In-house welding, finishing, and assembly", "Specializes in complex, multi-component instruments with tight tolerances", "Two US facilities in Mishawaka and Plymouth, Indiana", "Full-service sterilization coordination (EtO, gamma, e-beam)"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1968 as F&F Machine Specialties in Mishawaka, Indiana -> /about-us", "Rebranded to Complexus Medical; leadership under Michael Behrens -> /about-us", "2013 expansion doubled Mishawaka headquarters; second site added in Plymouth, Indiana in 2021 -> /about-us", "Full-