UPDATE companies SET description='The Valparaiso, Indiana facility began in 1979 as Custom Machining Services, establishing itself as a key domestic source for hydraulic hose crimpers, crimping dies, and related hose equipment. Continental’s North American headquarters are located in Culpeper, Virginia.

The Valparaiso plant specializes in manufacturing hydraulic hose assembly equipment, including crimpers and dies, serving the fluid power distribution market. As part of Continental Corporation, the location operates alongside a broader U.S. manufacturing footprint that includes sites in Clinton, Mississippi; Fairlawn, Ohio; Fort Mill, South Carolina; Marysville, Ohio; Mount Vernon, Illinois; and Sumter, South Carolina. The company’s engineering and technology teams develop radar, sensor, and autonomous driving systems, with recent milestones such as 200 million radar units produced.

Primary customers include hydraulic hose distributors and original equipment manufacturers in the fluid power sector. Through its automotive division—soon to be rebranded as Aumovio—Continental supplies advanced driver-assistance systems to global automakers. Strategic partnerships with Aurora Innovation and NVIDIA aim to deploy driverless trucks at scale, while collaboration with trinamiX on biometric sensing displays earned a CES Innovation Award.

Continental states that its Valparaiso operation distinguishes itself as one of the U.S. producers of hydraulic hose crimping equipment. The corporation emphasizes a mission of advancing safety technologies to get people “SafelyThere,” guided by core values of trust, passion to win, freedom to act, and mutual accountability. The Indiana plant also runs a state-recognized machinist apprenticeship and an assembly technician seal certification program.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Hydraulic hose crimper manufacturing", "Crimping die manufacturing", "Hose equipment assembly", "Customer service", "Radar and sensor production", "Autonomous driving system development", "Software engineering", "Machinist apprenticeship training", "Assembly technician certification training"], "industries": ["Hydraulic hose industry", "Automotive", "Autonomous vehicle technology", "Fluid power distribution", "Commercial vehicle technology"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["One of the leading U.S. producers of hydraulic hose crimpers, crimping dies, and hose equipment solutions", "200 million radar units produced for automotive safety systems", "Long-term manufacturing partnership with Aurora and NVIDIA for driverless truck deployment", "CES Innovation Award Honoree for invisible biometric sensing display with trinamiX", "Indiana Department of Labor-recognized machinist apprenticeship and assembly tech seal certification"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1979 as Custom Machining Services in Valparaiso, Indiana -> db description", "Continental acquired Valparaiso plant November 1, 2017 -> db description", "Valparaiso plant has 100 employees -> db description, db employee_count", "Valparaiso plant produces hydraulic hose crimpers, crimping dies, hose equipment solutions -> db description", "Headquarters in Culpeper, Virginia -> db hq_city, hq_state_label", "Multiple U.S. manufacturing locations listed -> 