UPDATE companies SET description='Contraxx Furniture operates from McConnelsville, Ohio, where it has been producing custom hospitality furniture for more than three decades. The company developed its distinctive hub-and-spoke manufacturing system in the 1990s, aiming to keep furniture production jobs in the United States by networking independent craft shops.

The company manufactures custom casegoods, seating, banquettes, tables, beds, and lobby furniture for hotels, resorts, restaurants, casinos, and senior-living communities. Its distributed model connects more than 45 family-owned factories specializing in woodworking, metal fabrication, stone work, upholstery, and finishing, with final assembly and finishing performed in two company-operated factories. Every piece undergoes a 15-point quality assurance inspection, and no minimum order quantities are required.

Contraxx serves designers, architects, developers, and FF&E professionals across North America. Projects include boutique hotels such as The Pearl in Nantucket, the Elliott House Boutique Hotel in Charleston, and the Sheraton Grand in Los Angeles, as well as restaurants like Hank’s Seafood and 1587 Prime Steakhouse, and casino properties including Grand Casinos.

The company emphasizes its American-made supply chain, the flexibility of its hub-and-spoke network to handle projects of any scale, and a collaborative approach that preserves design intent from early engineering through installation. It positions itself as a partner for bespoke hospitality projects where custom design, craftsmanship, and reliable delivery are critical.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom wood furniture manufacturing", "Metal fabrication", "Stone furniture parts production", "Upholstery", "Finishing", "Assembly", "On-site field measurements", "Turnkey installation", "Product development", "Design engineering support", "Hub-and-spoke distributed manufacturing coordination", "15-point quality assurance inspection"], "industries": ["Hospitality", "Hotels", "Resorts", "Restaurants", "Casinos", "Senior Living", "Mixed-Use Developments", "Boutique Hotels", "Upscale Restaurants", "Bars", "Vacation Clubs", "Multi-family Developments", "Commercial Properties"], "materials": ["Wood", "Metal", "Stone", "Upholstery fabrics", "Finishes"], "equipment": [], "volume": "1 to 1,000 units", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Hub-and-spoke manufacturing network of 45+ family-owned factories", "No minimum order quantities", "15-point quality assurance inspection on every product", "Made exclusively in the United States with no offshore production", "Turnkey installation and on-site field measurement services"], "facts_used": ["Location: McConnelsville, Ohio -> db", "Operating for more than three decades -> /", "Hub-and-spoke system created in the 1990s -> /about-us", "Network of 45+ family-owned factories -> /about-us", "Two state-of-the-art furniture factories -> /about-us", "5,000+ skilled jobs created -> /about-us", "Custom casegoods, seating, banquettes, tables, beds, lobby furniture -> /", "Woodworking, metal fabrication, stone, upholstery, finishing -> /about-us", "15-point quality assurance inspection -> /", "No minimum order quantities -> /", "Industries: hotels, resorts, restaurants, casinos, senior living, mixed-use -> /", "Customer types: designers, architects, developers, FF&E professionals -> /", "Project examples: The Pearl, Elliott House, Sheraton Grand, Hank''s Seafood, 1587 Prime Steakhouse, Grand Casinos -> /", "Made exclusively in America -> /", "Turnkey installation and on-site field measurements -> /", "Volume range: one to 1,000 units -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Contraxx is a high-quality American manufacturer of custom bar and restaurant furniture", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "No minimum order quantity", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='contraxx-furniture' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Control Components, Inc. operates from Pelham, Alabama, where it has spent 35 years supplying factory automation and machine safety products to industrial customers. The company is organized as an Alabama corporation and makes clear that it is not affiliated with the California-based IMI Critical Engineering, which also uses the CCI name. No founding year or individual founders are disclosed in public materials.

The business functions as an authorized distributor rather than a manufacturer. Its line card spans sensors (inductive, photoelectric, ultrasonic, limit switches), machine safety (light curtains, scanners, mats, relays, interlock switches), control panel devices (timers, relays, contactors, circuit breakers, terminal blocks, pushbuttons), industrial communication (Ethernet switches), and process measurement instruments. Staff described as factory-trained assist customers in selecting what the company calls the most cost-effective products for each application.

Primary markets include automotive, general industrial, original equipment manufacturers, and systems integrators. The distributor holds authorized status for brands such as ABB, GE, IDEC, Eaton Cutler-Hammer, Balluff, Pepperl+Fuchs, Schmersal, and dozens of others listed across its catalog.

