UPDATE companies SET description='Conway Corp has operated from Conway, Arkansas since 1929, when city leaders signed a charter on May 6 to create the Conway Corporation. The municipal utility was formed to take over the city''s electric light plant and, by 1930, its waterworks and sewer plant.

The corporation provides electric, water, wastewater, video, internet, voice, and security services to residential and business customers across the Conway area. Its infrastructure includes the Stone Dam Creek Wastewater Treatment Plant, the James H. Crews operate 24 hours a day, 365 days a year, and the company launched one of the earliest broadband cable internet services in the country in 1997.

Customers range from individual households to local businesses and the broader Conway community. The utility serves the city''s residential neighborhoods, commercial districts, and a designated Data District where gigabit internet was first rolled out to businesses. It also supports economic development initiatives and education programs as part of its community mandate.

The company states it was founded on a commitment to the community where its employees live and work. Its core values — customer satisfaction, innovation, safety, reliability, responsibility, and community — are framed as the reason it exists, with a focus on delivering safe, affordable, and environmentally sound services while maintaining fiscal stewardship.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Electric power distribution", "Water treatment and distribution", "Wastewater collection and treatment", "Cable television (IPTV streaming via ConwayCorpTV)", "High-speed internet (up to 1 Gbps)", "Digital voice/telephone service", "Security and automation systems", "Solar energy programs", "GIS mapping and infrastructure management", "Customer service and billing (myConwayCorp portal)"], "industries": ["Residential utilities", "Commercial utilities", "Municipal government services", "Telecommunications", "Economic development"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": [], "facts_used": ["Founded 1929 via city charter -> /about", "Headquarters Conway, Arkansas -> /about, db", "Municipal nonprofit ownership -> /about", "Services: electric, water, wastewater, video, internet, voice, security -> /about, /", "24/7/365 operations -> /about", "Early broadband internet 1997 -> /about", "Gigabit internet for Data District and residential -> /about, /", "Stone Dam Creek Wastewater Treatment Plant -> /about", "James H. Brewer Lake reservoir -> /about", "Gleason Water Treatment Plant -> /about", "Fiber-coax hybrid network -> /about", "Core values and mission -> /about", "Community-focused founding purpose -> /about, db"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Conway Corp is proud to provide electric, water, wastewater, video, internet, voice and security services for our fellow community members.", "founded_year": "1929", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": 