UPDATE companies SET description='Corporate Creations was founded in 1995 in Omaha, Nebraska, by Wade Lewis while he was an undergraduate at the University of Nebraska at Omaha. Lewis initially launched Greek Creations to serve fraternity and sorority merchandise needs, and the success of that venture led friends and family to request similar custom screen printing, embroidery, and promotional products for their own organizations. Corporate Creations was born from that demand and remains headquartered at 9001 F Street in Omaha, serving the surrounding metro communities including Ralston, Bellevue, Millard, Elkhorn, LaVista, and Papillion.

The company provides custom decoration services centered on screen printing and embroidery, supplemented by a promotional product sourcing program that offers access to over 700,000 items. In-house capabilities include graphic design, digitizing for embroidery, art proofing with a 48-hour turnaround, and rush production options. Orders are produced at their Omaha facility with typical lead times of 10 business days after art approval. Minimum order quantities are set at six pieces for embroidery, 12 pieces for screen printing, and 100 pieces for most promotional products, though embroidery reorders carry no minimum.

Corporate Creations serves a broad base of local clients: businesses, clubs, sports teams, churches, charities, schools, universities, and non‑profit organizations throughout the Omaha metro area. Customers range from small community groups to larger corporate accounts, all receiving the same design‑to‑delivery workflow.

The business was started to simplify and improve the way groups purchased custom merchandise, and that mission persists in a focus on low minimums, transparent pricing, and a collaborative art process that includes two free revisions. The company highlights its award‑winning design team and its recognition as Omaha Magazine’s Best of Omaha Custom T‑Shirt Store winner from 2021 through 2025 as evidence of its service quality.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Screen printing", "Embroidery", "Promotional product sourcing", "Custom graphic design", "Art proofing", "Digitizing", "Rush production", "Reorder management"], "industries": ["Businesses", "Clubs", "Sports teams", "Churches", "Charities", "Schools", "Universities", "Non-profit organizations", "Fraternities and sororities"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "Typically 10 business days for production; art proof within 48 hours", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Low minimum order quantities (6 for embroidery, 12 for screen printing, 100 for promotional products)", "Standard 10\u2011business\u2011day production turnaround", "Rush production services available for tight deadlines", "Art proof delivered within 48 hours with two free revisions", "Embroidery reorders require no minimum quantity"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1995 by Wade Lewis in Omaha, NE -> /about-us", "Headquarters at 9001 F Street, Omaha, NE 68127 -> /", "Services: screen printing, embroidery, promotional products -> /", "Minimum orders: embroidery 6, screen printing 12, promo 100 -> /", "Typical production turnaround 10 business days -> /", "Art proof within 48 hours, two revisions included -> /", "Embroidery reorders have no minimums -> /", "Serves businesses, clubs, teams, churches, charities, schools, non-profits -> /", "Best of Omaha Winner 2021-2025 -> /", "Founder started Greek Creations for fraternity/sorority merchandise -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "specializes in custom screen printing, embroidery and promotional products", "founded_year": "1995", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "Embroidery: 6 pieces; Screen printing: 12 pieces; Promotional products: 100 pieces", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='corporate-creations' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Corporate Woodworking, Inc. (CWI) operates from Fairfield, New Jersey, as part of the Andersen Companies group founded by Dan Andersen. Andersen began his career in 1974 working from his basement after experience as an estimator and project manager in New York and New Jersey. He incorporated the Andersen Corporation, grew it significantly, then sold it in 1986 to start Andersen Interior Contracting. In 1989 he launched Corporate Woodworking as a dedicated high‑end architectural woodworking firm, bringing over key staff from his earlier ventures.

CWI specializes in custom architectural millwork, handling engineering, fabrication, and installation of reception areas, wall paneling (including exotic and blueprint‑matched veneers and opaque lacquer finishes), doors and sidelights, and pantry/cafe/servery units. The shop produces thousands of square feet of paneling and thousands of door systems annually, though facility size and headcount are not disclosed.

The company serves the commercial construction industry, supplying corporate offices, institutional projects, and other interior build‑outs where high‑quality millwork is required.

CWI differentiates itself through the “Andersen Way” — a philosophy built on relationships, integrity, agility, teamwork, and efficiency — and through its participation in the Architectural Woodwork Institute’s Quality Certification Program (QCP), which validates adherence to stringent design and manufacturing standards.', certifications=ARRAY['AWI Quality Certification Program (QCP)','Architectural Woodwork Institute (AWI) member']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom architectural millwork", "Architectural woodworking", "Reception area fabrication and installation", "Wall paneling (exotic veneers, blueprint-matched veneers, opaque lacquer finishes)", "Doors and sidelights coordination, fabrication, and installation", "Pantry, cafe, and servery fabrication and installation", "Engineering and coordination of millwork packages", "AWI QCP certified manufacturing"], "industries": ["Commercial construction", "Corporate office interiors"], "materials": ["Exotic veneers", "Blueprint-matched veneers", "Opaque lacquer finishes", "Wood"], "equipment": [], "volume": "Thousands of square feet of panels and thousands of door systems annually", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["AWI Quality Certification Program (QCP) certified", "Thousands of square feet of paneling and thousands of door systems installed annually", "The Andersen Way philosophy: relationships, integrity, agility, teamwork, efficiency", "Part of the Andersen Companies with affiliate Andersen Interior Contracting", "Single-source engineering, fabrication, and installation for complex millwork"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1989 by Dan Andersen -> /about", "Headquartered in Fairfield, New Jersey -> db", "Part of Andersen Companies with affiliate Andersen Interior Contracting -> /", "AWI member and QCP certified -> /", "Produces thousands of square feet of paneling and thousands of door systems annually -> /", "Specializes in reception areas, wall paneling, doors & sidelights, pantries -> /", "Serves commercial construction industry -> /about", "Philosophy: The Andersen Way (Relationships, Integrity, Agility, Teamwork, Efficiency) -> /about", "Dan Andersen started in basement in 1974, founded Andersen Corporation, sold 1986, started Andersen Interior Contracting, then Corporate Woodworking in 1989 -> /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "When your project involves custom architectural woodworking and requires the use of a firm that can deliver and install the highest quality product", "founded_year": "1989", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/andersen-companies/"], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='corporate-woodworking-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Corteco USA operates from Milan, Ohio, as the North American aftermarket arm of the Freudenberg Group, a global technology company. The business supplies spare parts to independent repair garages and distributors, leveraging the Freudenberg portfolio of original-equipment components.

The company offers a catalog of more than 26,000 products across four main categories: sealing solutions such as oil seals and gaskets (including the Simmerring® brand), rubber-to-metal components for vibration control, steering and suspension parts numbering over 7,000 references, and cabin air filtration with roughly 850 filter variations. Customers access the range through an online catalog (ecatcorteco.com) and a dedicated seal-finder tool (findyourseal.com).

Corteco serves the independent automotive aftermarket, targeting passenger cars, heavy-duty trucks, two-wheelers, and emerging e-mobility platforms. Its parts are sold to independent garages and wholesale distributors worldwide.

